id: pm-todos-tnou
title: Packed acceptance reports a bare timeout without scenario or subprocess diagnostics
description: "Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-todos#165 (filed 2026-10-28, missed by the blind issue watch). scripts/accept-packed.ts on current main still throws only '<command> exceeded <deadline>ms and was terminated' in its ETIMEDOUT branch (line ~80): it drops the captured stdout/stderr and the scenario name, so a hung 'bun init -y' (observed once on release PR #164's Node 26 job, 2026-10-28) cannot be diagnosed — no scenario, no output, no environment hint. The releases themselves have since succeeded (v2026.10.29 through v2026.10.31 green), so this is the remaining diagnostic gap, not a release blocker: include the scenario name and captured output in timeout errors and fail closed with the scenario list when a scenario never starts."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,diagnostics,"gh:unbraind/pm-todos#165"
created_at: "2026-11-02T09:18:44.778Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T19:17:38.358Z"
author: pi-glm
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T15:12:19.018Z",codex-sol,"Issue 165 remains reproducible on main: the subprocess timeout branch drops captured output and scenario context, and receipts appear only after all scenarios succeed. Reuse this tagged item. Plan: deterministic real-process timeout regression in a non-git SDK tracker, shared bounded sanitized diagnostics for every subprocess, partial receipts and runtime context, unchanged five-minute production timeout and all six current scenarios. Historical Bun hang cause and repeatability remain unknown."
  "2026-11-06T15:15:59.004Z",codex-sol,"Failing-first proof: the original timeout behavior fails the real subprocess regression (0/1) because the diagnostic has no bun-current scenario. The corrected runner passes 5/5 targeted tests, including a real non-git SDK tracker, timeout termination, nonzero exit, missing executable, bounded privacy-preserving previews, exact matrix completion, and the actual entrypoint failure report. npm run build:test, npm run typecheck and npm run docstring pass; this repository has no separate lint script."
  "2026-11-06T15:18:02.757Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral reverts were run only in disposable copies. Reverting runPackedCommand to the original subprocess behavior fails 3/5 tests; replacing summarizePackedOutput with raw passthrough fails 4/5; removing packedMatrixReport completion enforcement fails 1/5; restoring the entrypoint throw-only failure path fails its focused test 1/1. All reverted implementations were discarded, and the fixed targeted suite passed again. Linked pm test run passed 5/5; automatic result tracking is disabled by project policy, so this comment records the receipt. Tracker commands use the pinned CLI 2026.11.4; the public registry reports 2026.11.6, and dependencies remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-06T15:23:24.166Z",codex-sol,"The npm-only Bun probe guard also fails its focused entrypoint test on behavioral revert (0/1). Local targeted tests, typechecking, test compilation, docstrings, changelog verification, privacy review and append-only history checks pass. An additional isolated-HOME npm release:check run reached the unchanged full coverage suite but was deliberately stopped because of shared-host load; it is not passing full-gate evidence. Per the task, CI will run both complete npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds. The underlying historical Bun hang remains unexplained; this change fixes its demonstrated diagnostic gap and preserves every current consumer."
  "2026-11-06T15:32:14.366Z",codex-sol,"Round 1 CI review found a CodeQL improper-sanitization warning in the disposable test preload generated with an interpolated fixture path. Replace it with static JavaScript deriving the launcher from the test entrypoint; pass private fixture text as child arguments instead of generating executable source from data. The diagnostic implementation is unchanged. Verify the targeted suite again and push this correction with tracker evidence, then requeue review."
  "2026-11-06T15:33:50.478Z",codex-sol,"The static-preload correction passes 5/5 targeted tests plus npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring and git diff --check. The same diagnostic suite also passed 5/5 on local Node 26.13.0 and Node 22.23.4 before the fixture-only refactor. CodeQL alert 13 on the prior head provides the failing static-analysis evidence; the next exact-head scan must clear it. Release claim without closing, regenerate changelog after this final tracker write, push with the test change, reply to review thread PRRT_kwDOSZpews60kTk8, and requeue current-head review."
  "2026-11-06T15:42:25.640Z",codex-sol,"Self-review found that the new sanitized top-level handler would hide the existing reason of non-subprocess validation failures. Preserve fixed validation identifiers rather than raw error messages, including unknown scenario and matrix fixture assertions. Add a failing entrypoint regression before the correction; arbitrary JSON or fixture text must still remain private."
  "2026-11-06T15:48:20.674Z",codex-sol,"Final self-review correction: trusted validation assertions now retain fixed reasons, while arbitrary parser and filesystem messages stay private. The unknown-scenario regression failed first (0/1) and now passes. Final targeted and linked pm test runs both pass 6/6; typecheck, test compilation and docstrings pass. Updated disposable behavioral reverts: original subprocess behavior fails 3/6, raw stream passthrough 4/6, missing completion guard 1/6, missing validation context 2/6; throw-only entrypoint and unconditional Bun probe each fail their focused test 1/1. Restoring the implementation passes 6/6 again. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/185 contains the item link, full evidence and CodeQL thread resolution. Current-head npm/Bun CI and CodeRabbit review remain required; superseded runs are not certification. Keep the item in progress and release the claim for verification."
  "2026-11-06T17:21:27.010Z",codex-sol,"Final verification for https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/185 on public head 16e33cac7c35b9ff21b5a4f081fc56bd560109d8: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/42246713552 passed both npm run release:check and bun run release:check on Node 22.18.0 and Node 26.13.0. Every path passed 475/475 tests and 6/6 packed consumers: 24 complete current-head receipts. Coverage for all 10 configured production files passed unchanged 97/93/98 thresholds. All four matrices produced SHA-256 689e4fd9ddc1f104c41e9617d3363f0ff57ca9d47f07a99397ba0e50b758c4a8. CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/42246713554 passed, alert 13 is fixed, and thread PRRT_kwDOSZpews60kTk8 is answered and resolved. Original immutable head f35cd942e277f96411d2442abb40a3e3b1572733 also passed its unmodified packed acceptance 4/4 with unchanged tracked source, Node 26.13.0, npm 11.20.0 and Bun 1.3.5, using original SDK hosts 2026.10.24 and 2026.10.20. This historical packed-only qualification differs from the original Node 26.12.1/Bun 1.4.4 environment; the original hang cause and repeatability remain unknown. Full receipts are in the PR. The required CodeRabbit wait reached 90 minutes without a completed review: zero completed rounds, queue entry retained, no approval inferred. Final PR state has zero failed or pending CI checks, zero unresolved threads and zero unvoted bot comments. Item remains in progress and unclaimed for orchestrator verification. This final receipt is held locally for a future code-fix push, following the review-loop prohibition on separate PM-only pushes."
  "2026-11-06T19:12:44.253Z",codex-sol,"Resumed PR 185 after CodeRabbit reviewed head 16e33ca and posted one actionable finding: preserve safe ENOENT and EACCES startup error codes without exposing exception messages. Reviewed the complete review body; no outside-diff or nitpick findings were present. Reuse this item and retain previous completed verification. The earlier receipt commit cc28152 remains local and will be pushed with this correction under the updated instruction to publish all commits. Canonical checkout dependencies were stale and have now been refreshed to the pinned CLI before tracker writes."
  "2026-11-06T19:15:45.162Z",codex-sol,"CodeRabbit finding PRRT_kwDOSZpews60ovCW is valid: PackedCommandError discarded safe startup error identities. Added a failing-first real-process regression using a missing executable, an owned non-executable fixture, and a non-directory working directory. It failed 0/1 before the fix, then passed with ENOENT and EACCES preserved and unlisted ENOTDIR kept generic. Only the four allowlisted codes are emitted; exception messages, paths and fixture data remain omitted. Behavioral mutation proofs in disposable copies independently removing ENOENT, removing EACCES, or exposing arbitrary error codes each fail the focused test 0/1. Restoring the fix passes 7/7 targeted tests. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring and git diff --check pass. README documents the safe codes; no deadlines, buffers, consumers, dependencies or thresholds changed."
  "2026-11-06T19:17:28.782Z",codex-sol,"Linked pm test run passed 7/7 with zero failures or skips; automatic linked-result tracking remains disabled by project policy. The new startup-code regression independently fails when either ENOENT or EACCES handling is reverted and when unknown codes are exposed. All disposable copies were removed; fixed tests pass after restoration. Release claim without closing and regenerate changelog after this final tracker write. Push both the prior receipt commit cc28152 and this code correction, reply to PRRT_kwDOSZpews60ovCW, and requeue CodeRabbit immediately. Fresh exact-head CI and review results will be retained in PR 185; prior head 16e33ca evidence is historical, not certification of the next head."
